From 2662f188e9af7661f5a16f309d9376fe1ac0417c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvia420-bit <salvia420@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/28] Vehicles (holtburger fork): harden Tick/dt and energy
 guards across Deployables and AirDefense

Hardens remaining sibling Tick/AdvanceRise/dt and energy mutation methods against non-positive, NaN, and infinite inputs:
- MissileTurretDeployable.AdvanceRise / Tick, MortarTurretDeployable.Tick, LaserTurretDeployable.Tick, GroundRadarDeployable.Tick, DeployableManager.Tick, AirDefenseManager.Tick, VehicleManager.Tick(double): reject !double.IsFinite(...) || <= 0.0 (and !float.IsFinite(dt) || dt <= 0.0f).
- IsoContainerDeployable.Tick: upgrade double.IsNaN to !double.IsFinite so +Infinity cannot snap DoorProgress in a single tick.
- VehicleManager.TickInner: clamp !double.IsFinite(elapsed) || elapsed < 0.0 to 0.0 alongside the 5.0s ceiling.
- BatteryDeployable.Charge / TryDischarge: reject non-finite and negative/zero joule inputs.
- Added 8 regression tests in DeployableEcosystemTests covering all guards and post-invalid-tick progression.

Verified with dotnet test ACE.Server.Tests (Vehicles|Landblock): 364/364 passed.
